<title>USA: Snyder Communications buys marketing firms.</title>
<headline>Snyder Communications buys marketing firms.</headline>
<dateline>BETHESDA, Md. 1997-07-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Snyder Communications Inc, which provides targeted marketing solutions, said on Tuesday it bought Sampling Corp of America and British-based Bounty Group Holdings Ltd, for undisclosed terms.</p>
<p>Sampling Corp provides targeted sampling programs for large companies while Bounty Group, located in Diss, England, is a product sampling company focused on new mothers.</p>
<p>Both deals are expected to be accretive to 1997 earnings, the company said. They would be accounted for as pooling of interests transactions.</p>
<p>((New York newsdesk 212-859-1730))</p>
</text>
